From: Tran Ha Tam <tranhatam@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Apr 2026 15:58:30 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] mail-core(wave2-auth): ship 4-flow auth content artifact + 9
 tests
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes BLK-PAYEMAIL-005 and partial DEC-PAYEMAIL-003 from
TEAM_PAYEMAIL_BLOCKERS_AND_DECISIONS_REQUIRED_2026-04-26.md.

Wave 2 auth content artifact mirrors the Wave 2 internal-alerts pattern
(wave2-internal-alerts.ts) so Team Auth can compose its own trigger
wiring on top.

Files:
- packages/mail-core/src/wave2-auth-templates.ts (NEW, 568 lines):
  4 builders (buildMagicLinkLoginPayload, buildResetPasswordPayload,
  buildEmailVerificationPayload, buildSecurityNoticePayload) + per-flow
  Input interfaces + DEFAULT_AUTH_TTL_POLICY (10/30/1440/0 minutes) +
  SecurityNoticeEventType union (7 events: new_device_login,
  password_changed, email_changed, mfa_enabled, mfa_disabled,
  account_locked, suspicious_activity). Bilingual VI/EN subject + text +
  HTML wrapper. HTML escapes user-controlled inputs. Empty-recipients
  guard throws explicit error. messageIdempotencyKey shape:
  `${flowCode}:${recipientEmail}:${submittedAt}`. Headers add
  `x-iai-auth-flow` so downstream consumers can route on flow code.
- packages/mail-core/src/index.ts: re-export wave2-auth-templates module.
- tests/integration/wave2-auth-templates.test.mjs (NEW, 9 tests):
  TTL policy lock, magic-link VI default, magic-link EN locale flip,
  reset-password safety reassurance, email-verification url, security
  notice with full context, all 7 security event labels, HTML escape,
  empty recipients reject. 9/9 PASS.

Verified:
- pnpm --filter @iai/mail-core build -> clean typecheck
- node --test tests/integration/wave2-auth-templates.test.mjs -> 9/9 PASS
- pnpm test:pay -> 59/59 PASS (no regression)
- pnpm test:mail-smtp -> 16/16 PASS
- pnpm test:mail-worker -> 3/3 PASS

Team Auth can now consume buildMagicLinkLoginPayload(...) etc. and
submit via mail.iai.one mail-api. Trigger wiring (when to call) remains
Team Auth's responsibility per AI Owner plan §1.3.

ack: IAI_ONE_PAYEMAIL_Q1_Q2_EXPANSION_BRIEF_2026-04-26 (Wave 2 content)

